35
00:04:18.597 --> 00:04:27.239
hid the note in it. "We will wait to see how Lupin replies," he said with a sharp glint

36
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.564
in his eye. Then the three men left the cell. That evening Lupin finished his meal and a

37
00:04:32.565 --> 00:04:41.398
guard retrieved his tray. Just outside the cell, however, Folenfant intercepted it and took it to Dudouis. "Check everything,"

38
00:04:41.399 --> 00:04:46.485
the police chief ordered. "Lupin’s reply will be here somewhere." They examined the dishes, the tray, and the utensils.

39
00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:52.818
Suddenly Dudouis let out a cry of joy. Inside the wooden handle of the knife was a piece of

40
00:04:52.819 --> 00:04:58.231
paper. It read simply: Make sure that H-P follows at a distance every day. I will go ahead.

41
00:04:58.232 --> 00:05:06.056
Thank you, dear friend. "At last!" cried Monsieur Dudouis gleefully. "We have him! A little strategy on our part,

42
00:05:06.057 --> 00:05:19.951
and we will catch not only Arsène Lupin, but his associates as well." The police chief grabbed Folenfant’s hands,

43
00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:32.102
and they danced around the room. For several months Arsène Lupin had been transported weekly to appear before

44
00:05:32.103 --> 00:05:36.506
Judge Bouvier, who was overseeing his case. One day the famous prisoner ignored his own lawyer and comically confessed

45
00:05:36.507 --> 00:05:44.847
to every charge against him: burglaries in a dozen neighborhoods, counterfeiting, and a bank robbery. "I confess I did

46
00:05:44.848 --> 00:05:58.490
everything, and there is ten times as much that you know nothing about," said Lupin. Frustrated by Lupin’s arrogance,

47
00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:07.339
the judge refused to see the thief again until he agreed to get serious about his upcoming trial.

48
00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:16.569
But when Dudouis showed the judge Lupin’s secret messages, Bouvier exploded in anger. "Bring that man back into my

49
00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:23.458
court!" the judge roared. "Monsieur Dudouis, I solemnly order you to do whatever is necessary to prevent his escape!"

50
00:06:23.459 --> 00:06:33.880
"As you wish, Judge," said Dudouis. "Starting tomorrow," continued Bouvier, "I want to see Lupin every day until he

51
00:06:33.881 --> 00:06:36.983
tells me what I want to know." The two men shook hands. So Lupin was taken to the

52
00:06:36.984 --> 00:06:47.213
judge every day with the other prisoners. All prisoners going to the courthouse were transported in the morning in

53
00:06:47.214 --> 00:06:52.777
horse-drawn police vans. These vans were nicknamed salad baskets because each van was divided into ten small cells, or

54
00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:59.110
baskets, five on each side. These cells, one for every prisoner, were constructed with iron bars, and riding

55
00:06:59.111 --> 00:07:09.118
in them was very uncomfortable. The prisoners usually left the courthouse after lunch and returned to Santé Prison between

56
00:07:09.119 --> 00:07:17.181
three and four, but one afternoon a decision was made to take Arsène Lupin back to the prison alone

57
00:07:17.182 --> 00:07:33.332
since the other prisoners had been delayed in court. "Choose any seat you like," said the guard to Lupin,

58
00:07:33.333 --> 00:07:41.761
laughing. Then the guard shut the door and climbed up into the driver’s seat. Once inside the van,

59
00:07:41.762 --> 00:07:51.157
Lupin moved to the third cell on his right and sat down. Soon the van began to move. "Where

60
00:07:51.158 --> 00:08:02.482
is that plate?" Lupin whispered to himself. He searched the floor with his right foot. "Ah, here it is.

61
00:08:02.483 --> 00:08:09.649
Now I press down on it . . ." The plate opened to reveal the street going by and

62
00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:17.466
two of the van’s wheels. Suddenly the van stopped. Loud, angry voices erupted from outside━a sick horse was

63
00:08:17.467 --> 00:08:24.951
blocking traffic, including another police van. Lupin took that moment to squeeze out of the hole in the bottom

64
00:08:24.952 --> 00:08:31.855
of the van and leap to the ground. He was free! Looking around, Lupin saw that two wagons had

65
00:08:31.856 --> 00:08:37.626
collided and angry drivers were about to come to blows. A block away a coachman saw Lupin drop out

66
00:08:37.627 --> 00:08:43.540
of the prison van and start to run. The coachman tried to alert the guard, but his voice

67
00:08:43.541 --> 00:08:50.563
